<title>UK: Northern Electric falls in active trade.</title>
<headline>Northern Electric falls in active trade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in hostile UK bid target Northern Electric were actively traded on Thursday as sources said U.S. predator CalEnergy was picking up the stock.</p>
<p>The shares fell 5-1/2p to 625p by 1152 GMT, in trade of seven million shares.</p>
<p>Sources said U.S. group CalEnergy is taking advantage of the weaker share price to raise its stake in the regional electricity company.</p>
<p>CalEnergy's offer price for Northern Electric shares is 630p but the UK company has urged its shareholders not to sell.</p>
<p>--Elaine Hardcastle, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4027</p>
